WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.310
- Back when the British
empire was colonizing

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:06.390
all of this land, they drew a line.

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:09.570
The line went right along
this little mountain range

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.390
and it was meant as a boundary.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:12.640
Back in London, there were saying

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.670
that no English settler was allowed

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:17.066
to settle West of this line.

00:00:17.066 --> 00:00:20.010
The British empire did this
because they were worried

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:23.100
that if settlers started
to expand into the West

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.440
they would bring the British Empire

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.780
into a war with native populations.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.210
They also didn't wanna
unnecessarily piss off France

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.710
who also had land in the West.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.840
So they told their settlers to settle,

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.470
but not pass this line.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.252
And then the settlers
completely ignored it.

00:00:37.252 --> 00:00:39.835
(upbeat music)

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:46.240
These settlers would
eventually declare independence

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.276
from Britain and start their own country.

00:00:48.276 --> 00:00:51.101
And from there the flood gates were open

00:00:51.101 --> 00:00:52.760
for westward expansion.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.888
- [Announcer] A frontier
people had remade a continent.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.950
Virtually all productive land
had been put to the plough.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.971
A free and independent
way of life prevail.

00:01:00.971 --> 00:01:02.830
(upbeat music)

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.310
- This westward blitz
was made possible through

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:08.000
the mass slaughter of people
who were living on this land,

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.240
which this little time lapse ignores.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.830
How that all went down will be
the subject of another video.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.820
But right now I want to
talk about what happened

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.158
when the U.S. got here.

00:01:16.158 --> 00:01:17.770
(upbeat music)

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:21.038
It's the mid 1800s and
the U.S has 27 States

00:01:21.038 --> 00:01:23.420
and a bunch of territories in the West,

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.490
but the country doesn't stretch from sea

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:27.090
to shining sea quite yet.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:28.687
At this point, they start to bump in to

00:01:28.687 --> 00:01:31.659
the recently independent
country of Mexico.

00:01:31.659 --> 00:01:34.150
(upbeat music)

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:37.850
The Northern part of Mexico
was called Tejas or Texas,

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.941
and it was populated
mainly with native groups

00:01:39.941 --> 00:01:43.120
who had nothing to do
with the U.S. or Mexico.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.180
They had just been living
there for centuries.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.296
So Mexico is looking at this

00:01:46.296 --> 00:01:49.249
fairly new sparsely populated
part of their country

00:01:49.249 --> 00:01:50.610
and thinking what you know,

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.150
what do we do with all this land?

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:54.480
They want to incentivize people to go with

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.880
and settle in this land

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.830
so it would potentially be
more economically productive

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.005
for the country of Mexico.

00:02:00.005 --> 00:02:01.560
So they made a plan.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.883
They started to rent huge swaths of land

00:02:03.883 --> 00:02:07.136
to American settlers so
that they would come in

00:02:07.136 --> 00:02:08.950
and settle the land.

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:10.770
And then return, these American settlers

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.851
would recruit more settlers
to come in and settle the land

00:02:13.851 --> 00:02:15.850
again, all with the hope that

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.110
it would benefit Mexico's
economy eventually.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:21.300
It did exactly the opposite.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.790
American settlers fled into Texas

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.260
onto this newly rented land,

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:27.260
just as the Mexican government hoped for,

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.235
but with them they brought slaves,

00:02:29.235 --> 00:02:32.020
which was totally illegal
in Mexico at the time.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.790
They also brought with them an attitude

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.168
of independence and frontier fever.

00:02:36.168 --> 00:02:40.050
This American obsession with
moving West to settle new land.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.019
- [Narrator] The westward movement,

00:02:41.019 --> 00:02:42.636
was like a great title wave.

00:02:42.636 --> 00:02:44.834
The odd corners were rapidly engulfed.

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:49.670
- Mexico soon realized that
this plan completely backfired

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.320
and that the Americans that
had rented land from them

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.700
were now not interested

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.560
in having Mexico as their government.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.553
So Mexico sends in the
military to remind the settlers

00:02:58.553 --> 00:03:00.750
that they're still in Mexico

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.805
and that they're technically
renting this land from Mexico.

00:03:03.805 --> 00:03:05.848
Well, this eventually escalated

00:03:05.848 --> 00:03:08.485
and they started to fight all out battles.

00:03:08.485 --> 00:03:10.363
And the American settlers lost.

00:03:10.363 --> 00:03:14.870
The big battle here was called
the Battle of the Alamo.

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.540
This guy, David Crockett, who was

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.240
like the symbol of Westward
expansion, died in this battle.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.432
And this loss spurred even more settlers

00:03:22.432 --> 00:03:26.310
to come to Texas and joined
the next fight against Mexico,

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.910
which the American settlers won.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:30.480
And with that, they declared a new nation

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.680
independent of Mexico,
the Republic of Texas.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.630
And now the map looks like this.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:38.120
A newly declared country
of American settlers

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.713
in between Mexico and the United States.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.860
But not everyone actually agreed

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:47.260
that the map looked like this.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.300
While Mexico conceded
that they lost the war.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.340
They disputed this map saying

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:54.670
that the border of the
new Republic of Texas

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:55.904
was actually here.

00:03:55.904 --> 00:03:59.260
And that all of this was still Mexico.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.743
So now you have a big land
dispute between Mexico

00:04:01.743 --> 00:04:03.750
and the Republic of Texas.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.014
Well soon it's 1845

00:04:05.014 --> 00:04:08.140
and Texas becomes the 28th
state of the United States.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.866
And yet this land is still disputed,

00:04:10.866 --> 00:04:12.690
but now it's a land dispute

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.743
between the United States
of America and Mexico.

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:20.311
Let's keep in mind that
despite all of this map drawing

00:04:20.311 --> 00:04:23.360
there are still loads of
native peoples who've lived

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.240
on this land for years and
are now being suffocated

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.773
by all these nations
trying to take their land.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:31.490
Again, that's another episode

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:34.530
and it's an important episode
and I want to do it justice.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:36.700
But for now what happens next

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.623
in the Mexico story gets kind of nuts.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:45.850
And the reason it gets
kind of nuts is mainly

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:49.578
because of this guy,
president James K. Polk.

00:04:49.578 --> 00:04:51.370
James Polk wins the presidency

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:54.750
and comes into office with
a list of four big things

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.290
he wants to do.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:57.390
It's his big wishlist.

00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:00.872
At the top of this wishlist
is Polk desire to capture

00:05:00.872 --> 00:05:03.580
this very specific part of Mexico,

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:05.200
which is called California.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.240
Remember that at the time, the
U.S. didn't actually stretch

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.980
from the Atlantic to the Pacific.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:12.890
The U.S. had colonized
portions of Oregon territory,

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:14.275
but it was kind of confusing

00:05:14.275 --> 00:05:16.270
because there were kind of
competing with the French

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:19.140
and the British, and they
didn't actually own it yet.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:22.627
But you'll notice that Oregon
was also on Polk's shortlist,

00:05:22.627 --> 00:05:24.699
but first California.

00:05:24.699 --> 00:05:28.150
He first tried to buy
California from Mexico

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:29.392
for $25 million.

00:05:29.392 --> 00:05:32.340
Mexico flat out said no.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:35.393
So Polk decides to pull
an incredibly dirty move.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:41.091
Remember this big old
swath of disputed territory

00:05:41.091 --> 00:05:42.620
that the U S inherited

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:44.430
when they admitted Texas into the union,

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:47.320
James Polk was pissed off that
Mexico didn't take his offer

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.153
to buy California.

00:05:48.153 --> 00:05:51.131
So he sends a small group of troops

00:05:51.131 --> 00:05:53.110
into this disputed territory

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.675
and has the March right up to here,

00:05:55.675 --> 00:05:57.690
right across from the river

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.510
that separates what
everyone agrees is Mexico.

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:03.430
But according to Mexico,
they've already been in Mexico

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.830
as soon as they crossed
into this dispute territory,

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:07.820
which Mexico believes is theirs.

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:09.698
So the Mexican army is sent to respond

00:06:09.698 --> 00:06:12.170
to what looks like an oncoming attack

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.410
from the United States.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.500
This is exactly what Polk wanted.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:17.878
A group of 1,600 Mexican soldiers attack

00:06:17.878 --> 00:06:21.835
this small group of 80
Americans killing 11 of them

00:06:21.835 --> 00:06:23.690
and capturing the rest.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:26.350
They easily one, since
they were outnumbered

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:28.301
by like a magnitude of like 20.

00:06:28.301 --> 00:06:30.610
But this is exactly what Polk needed

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:31.820
to get his wishlist going.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.604
After this battle, Polk
goes to Congress and reports

00:06:34.604 --> 00:06:37.534
that the Mexicans have
quote, invaded our territory

00:06:37.534 --> 00:06:41.330
and shed American blood
upon American soil.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.070
Even though this wasn't
necessarily American soil;

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.550
it was disputed territory

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.830
that most people thought
was rightfully Mexico.

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:48.880
But it didn't matter.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:51.670
The death of Americans was
enough to rally Congress

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:53.873
around declaring war with Mexico.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:01.270
The U.S. easily won this war
and they did it pretty quickly.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:04.810
Remember that the taking
over of Texas was originally

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:08.013
a bunch of settlers who band
together, made a militia,

00:07:08.013 --> 00:07:09.845
fought Mexico on their own

00:07:09.845 --> 00:07:12.536
and declared the Republic of Texas.

00:07:12.536 --> 00:07:15.300
Not super great, but at least it wasn't

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.970
like a government leader
sending his soldiers in

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:21.033
that he knows, are going to
lose to provoke another country

00:07:21.033 --> 00:07:22.834
to kill those soldiers

00:07:22.834 --> 00:07:25.560
so that he can use democratic processes

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.445
and institutions to make war all so

00:07:27.445 --> 00:07:30.490
that he can take over
land from that country.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:33.760
I mean, Polk really wanted California.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.760
There were critics of this in the time.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.578
One of whom was this guy who
said that letting Polk force

00:07:38.578 --> 00:07:41.850
the country into war
with Mexico was quote,

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:44.430
allowing him to make war at pleasure.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.190
And Abe hit the nail on the head.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:48.417
This whole war was started and fought at

00:07:48.417 --> 00:07:51.960
the pleasure of this
president, James K. Polk.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.210
So anyway, the U S easily wins the war.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:56.361
They pay Mexico $15 million

00:07:56.361 --> 00:07:59.812
and Mexico gave up all of this.

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:02.538
As a part of this loss.
Mexico also conceded

00:08:02.538 --> 00:08:04.616
all of this disputed territory

00:08:04.616 --> 00:08:07.680
making it officially a part
of the U S state of Texas.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:10.879
The U.S. had grown significantly
in just a couple of years.

00:08:10.879 --> 00:08:13.470
And Polk got his California.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.400
The U.S.could have taken more land.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.210
Some American lawmakers at the time

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:18.840
wanted to take all of Mexico.

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:21.600
And militarily they likely
could have done this,

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:24.239
but they only took this part
of Mexico because it was

00:08:24.239 --> 00:08:28.470
the most sparsely populated
mainly by native Americans.

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:31.490
One Senator at the time, who
happened to be pro-slavery,

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.797
argued on the Senate floor
against taking all of Mexico.

00:08:34.797 --> 00:08:38.170
Saying quote, we have never
dreamt of incorporating

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:40.955
into the Union, any,
but the Caucasian race,

00:08:40.955 --> 00:08:43.060
the free white race.

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:45.979
Are we to associate with
ourselves as equal companions

00:08:45.979 --> 00:08:49.990
and fellow citizens, the Indians
and mixed races of Mexico?

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:51.735
In other words, let me put it plainly.

00:08:51.735 --> 00:08:55.681
The policy was let's search
for land where we exterminate

00:08:55.681 --> 00:08:58.110
the natives and settle white people

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:00.077
instead of let's take land

00:09:00.077 --> 00:09:01.886
where there's already big populations

00:09:01.886 --> 00:09:03.510
that are non white people

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:05.694
that we would have to
bring into our country.

00:09:05.694 --> 00:09:09.230
This is a policy that
informed American expansion

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:12.266
and imperialism for a very long time.

00:09:12.266 --> 00:09:15.434
And it's what guided a lot
of what land we took over

00:09:15.434 --> 00:09:17.533
and what land we didn't take over.

00:09:19.231 --> 00:09:22.071
Okay, so through this
unprovoked racially tinge war

00:09:22.071 --> 00:09:25.266
Polk checked off California from his list.

00:09:25.266 --> 00:09:26.690
And just the next month

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:28.830
Oregon was organized into a territory

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.550
after working out a deal with the British.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:33.340
Polk had exterminated anyone in his way.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.900
And now he had a coast to coast country.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:36.733
A few years later

00:09:36.733 --> 00:09:38.698
they bought this little
piece of land from Mexico

00:09:38.698 --> 00:09:42.280
and this completed the Southern
border that we know today.

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:44.332
One that was forged first from a rebellion

00:09:44.332 --> 00:09:45.606
of American settlers,

00:09:45.606 --> 00:09:48.521
then a war at the
pleasure of James K. Polk.

00:09:48.521 --> 00:09:51.300
And then finally that little
purchase there at the end.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:53.620
The native people and
Mexicans that lived here when

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:54.605
the U.S. took it over.

00:09:54.605 --> 00:09:58.010
And let's be clear on something
that is not a small number.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:59.920
They were predictably oppressed

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:02.190
as white settlers fled into this region

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:03.480
often looking for gold.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.470
Native people were driven from their land

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:08.129
and the rights of Mexican
property owners were erased in

00:10:08.129 --> 00:10:10.450
the name of a state constitution

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:12.010
that only let white people vote.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:14.290
- [Narrator] This land after
a little more than a century

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:16.782
and a half had become great nation,

00:10:16.782 --> 00:10:19.167
the United States of America.

00:10:19.167 --> 00:10:22.501
- So, the U S stole Mexico in the 1800s,

00:10:22.501 --> 00:10:26.088
partly because they opened
their borders to Americans

00:10:26.088 --> 00:10:28.221
to let them in to work their land,

00:10:28.221 --> 00:10:33.221
which is just a very
strange, full circle irony.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:38.660
Especially because today you
go to the U.S.-Mexico border

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.369
and we do everything to make it clear

00:10:41.369 --> 00:10:44.418
that this side of that wall is U.S.

00:10:44.418 --> 00:10:47.014
when just a few years
ago it was all Mexico.

00:10:47.014 --> 00:10:49.030
I wish like the Hawaii video

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:52.810
I had some high note to
end on here, but I don't.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:54.433
So, so yeah.

